# TODO_progress_display
#
# DAG progress visualization with "power flow" rendering.
# Replace verbose log-line dumps with a live DAG display showing nodes
# lighting up as execution progresses (SimCity 2013 power grid style).

## Problem

Current shell output dumps sequential `[node_name]` log lines with no
sense of overall progress, structure, or relationships. Long pipelines
produce walls of text that scroll off screen.

## Architecture

    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │  Layer 4: Renderers (terminal, CI, web future)  │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │  Layer 3: DagProgress (renderer-agnostic state) │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │  Layer 2: Frame loop + ProgressObserver         │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │  Layer 1: Symbol system (core/ir visual vocab)  │
    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Integrates with existing infrastructure:
- `Renderable` trait (core/ir/src/render.rs) — generated file headers
- Language SubDag module (core/ir/src/language/) — same compositional pattern
- CI rendering (core/ir/src/transport/ci/) — CiContext feeds into observer
- `to_mermaid()` (core/ir/src/dag.rs) — progress Mermaid via SemanticColor

