## Layer 4: Renderers

### Render modes (orthogonal to encoding tier)

```rust
enum RenderMode {
    Standard,   // Symbol-per-state, clean layout
    Dynamic,    // Cellular automaton effects, wavefront animation
    Compact,    // Single-line summary
}
```

### Terminal renderer

Carriage-return based (`\r` + `\x1b[{N}A` cursor-up). Zero dependencies.
Falls back to append-only when piped (not a TTY).

The terminal renderer implements FrameLoop:
- `update()`: processes observer events, advances animations (dynamic mode)
- `render()`: builds display lines from layout + symbols, writes to stdout

Layout: leveled from topo order, left-to-right, wrapping at terminal width.
See Appendix B for visual mockups.

### Dynamic mode

Purely a rendering concern — same DagProgress data model. Adds:
- Edge wavefront propagation (═══ spreading along edge path)
- Node state morph sequences (○ → ◔ → ◑ → ◐ for pending→running)
- 1D cellular automaton (Rule 110) on idle edges for ambient "alive" effect

Frame scheduling uses Adaptive policy: slows for visually interesting
transitions, catches up when execution is fast. See Appendix C.

### CI renderer

CiProgressObserver wraps CiContext — formalizes existing ad-hoc callbacks.
Uses ASCII tier. Maps SemanticColor to CI annotation levels.

### Web renderer (future, deferred)

DagProgress has Serialize → JSON/SSE to browser → Mermaid + style classes.
Zero changes to Layers 1-3 needed.

